{"resource":{"id":"react-quick-revision-notes","title":"React.js — Quick Revision Notes","category":"Web Development","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"10 min","pages":6,"lastUpdated":"February 2026","tags":["Web Development","React","Hooks"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Concise React.js revision notes optimized for interview prep and last-minute review — summaries, syntax references, comparison tables, and memory tricks."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"core","label":"Core Concepts"},{"id":"hooks","label":"Hooks Cheat Table"},{"id":"compare","label":"Comparison Tables"},{"id":"tricks","label":"Memory Tricks"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"React.js — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Web Development","time":"5 min"},{"title":"React.js — PDF Notes","tag":"Web Development","time":"63 min"},{"title":"React.js — Interview Questions","tag":"Web Development","time":"34 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Refresh every React essential in under 15 minutes.</li>\n          <li>Recall syntax and hook rules under interview pressure.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"core\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Core Concepts (One-liners)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>JSX:</strong> JS + HTML-like syntax, compiles to createElement.</li>\n          <li><strong>Component:</strong> function returning JSX.</li>\n          <li><strong>Props:</strong> read-only inputs.</li>\n          <li><strong>State:</strong> local mutable data; triggers re-render.</li>\n          <li><strong>Key:</strong> stable id for list items.</li>\n          <li><strong>Virtual DOM:</strong> in-memory tree, diffed to real DOM.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Render cycle: state change → virtual DOM diff → minimal DOM patch.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"hooks\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Hooks Cheat Table</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Hook</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Use</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useState</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Local state</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useEffect</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Side effects after render</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useRef</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Mutable value / DOM ref</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useMemo</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Memoize value</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useCallback</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Memoize function</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useContext</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Read Context</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\"><code>useReducer</code></td><td class=\"border p-2\">Complex state</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const [n, setN] = useState(0);\nuseEffect(() =&gt; { /* effect */ return () =&gt; { /* cleanup */ }; }, [dep]);</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"compare\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Comparison Tables</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">A</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">B</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Pick</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Context</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Redux</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Context for low-freq state</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">useMemo</td><td class=\"border p-2\">useCallback</td><td class=\"border p-2\">value vs function</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Controlled</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Uncontrolled</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Controlled by default</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — State management decision tree from local to global.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"tricks\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Memory Tricks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>SPUR:</strong> State, Props, Updater, Render — the render cycle.</li>\n          <li><strong>Keys never index:</strong> unless list is static.</li>\n          <li><strong>Effect = Sync:</strong> synchronize with external systems.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Missing dependency arrays in useEffect.</li>\n          <li>Mutating state directly.</li>\n          <li>Setting state during render.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rules of hooks, immutability, and stable keys — the three pillars that catch most bugs.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Why do effects fire twice in dev?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Strict Mode double-invokes to catch impure effects. It stops in production.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Revision notes — pair with hands-on practice.</p>\n      </div></section>"}